/* Paper-white card, per bible 10.1 and the handoff's token table.
 *
 * WAS A DARK CARD - rgba(20,20,24,.85) with near-white text. That is the
 * Era-2 clinical direction from specs/broodline_art_direction.md, which
 * bible 10.1 records as abandoned ("It is a good idea and it is not what got
 * built"). Every screen in the client had been styled to it, which is why
 * the app rendered as dark boxes. This file is the pattern the rest follow.
 *
 * ELEVATION IS THE SURFACE/PAPER CONTRAST, not a shadow: USS has no
 * box-shadow, and on a light theme white-on-paper is what reads as lifted.
 * See Theme.uss's header note 2.
 */
.creature-card {
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 160px;
    padding: 12px;
    /* 20px, the handoff's own `border-radius: 20px` at `Creature Roster
     * .dc.html:56`, and it is --radius-card exactly rather than a literal
     * near it - this tile IS a card. It was 18 for two phases with nothing
     * behind the number. */
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--divider);
}

/* The slot final art drops into. Three aligned layers from one bake camera:
 * body, then combat one at the dorsal socket, then combat two at the flank.
 *
 * 74px, WHICH IS THE HANDOFF'S OWN AND 10px MORE THAN THIS CARD CARRIED FOR
 * TWO PHASES. `Creature Roster.dc.html:59` is `height: 74px; display: grid;
 * place-items: center` around art drawn at 46-66px - so the tile's picture
 * is the biggest thing on it, which at 64 it was not. The card grows by 10px
 * and the two-column grid is unaffected: `.creature-card` is a fixed 160px
 * wide and only the row heights move.
 *
 * NO FILL. The handoff's roster tile draws its creature straight on the
 * card's own white, with no sunk plate behind it (`:59` sets only a height
 * and a centring) - the plate was this project's, and against six species it
 * read as a window each animal was posted through. The splice chamber's
 * parents keep a tinted disc because there it is `HeroSlot`'s ring and disc,
 * which the handoff DOES draw. */
.creature-card__slot {
    height: 74px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.creature-card__layer {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

/* THE HEADER IS THE GENERATION CHIP'S ROW AND NOTHING ELSE NOW, which is
 * the handoff's own card: `Creature Roster.dc.html:56-58` opens each tile
 * with a `justify-content: space-between` row holding the generation badge
 * and a status dot, ABOVE the art, and puts the name under the picture. The
 * name used to share this row with a bare `G4` label; it is a sibling below
 * the slot now, in the handoff's order.
 *
 * `space-between` IS KEPT FOR THE DOT THAT IS NOT DRAWN YET. The handoff's
 * right-hand mark is a per-creature status (`#6cba8b` on duty, `#e8b34a`
 * growing) and no DTO field carries it - Phase 9 Task 16's report names it.
 * A chip alone sits left either way, which is where it belongs. */
.creature-card__header {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
}

/* The chip host, cleared and refilled on every Bind - see CreatureCard.Bind
 * for why a GenChip cannot be re-pointed. Layout only; the chip brings its
 * own fill, radius, padding and `t-num`. */
.creature-card__gen { flex-direction: row; }

.creature-card__name {
    font-size: var(--text-card-title);
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: var(--ink);
}

/* The role line - bible 1.2's role word and the creature's Instinct, which
 * is the handoff's `Warform · on duty` at `Creature Roster.dc.html:64`:
 * 10px, 700, --mute. IT LOST ITS TRACKING AND ITS SHOUT in Phase 9 Task 16
 * and both were wrong before: `letter-spacing` plus `-unity-font-style:
 * bold` is the `.t-micro` treatment for an UPPERCASE eyebrow, and this is a
 * sentence in sentence case. Tracked out, "Wall · Forage" read as a label
 * for the row under it rather than as a description of the animal above. */
.creature-card__instinct {
    margin-top: 1px;
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
    color: var(--mute);
}

.creature-card__traits {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 7px;
}

/* VERTICAL ONLY. The handoff's `gap: 4px` at `Creature Roster.dc.html:65` is
 * already `TraitChip`'s own 2px-a-side margin; restating the horizontal half
 * here made every chip 6px wider than it measures and wrapped both of them
 * onto separate rows inside a 136px tile. USS on 6000.6.0f1 has no `gap`, so
 * the between-rows half has nowhere else to live.
 *
 * --space-1 RATHER THAN THE LITERAL 4px IT WAS - Phase 9 Task 16b. The
 * identical declaration is written in `SpliceChamberView.uss` for the
 * identical gap under the identical chips, and it was written there as the
 * token: one gap reading as "the handoff's 4" in one file and "the scale's
 * first step" in another is the same number pretending to be two. The token
 * wins because the value IS on the scale and because this phase's standing
 * rule is that spacing comes from Tokens.uss. `TraitChip`'s own 2px stays a
 * literal - there is no 2px step to name it with. */
.creature-card__traits > .trait-chip { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }

/* bible 3.3: the Founder's name is what stops a player. A visible marker on
 * the card itself is the read that carries into the roster and the splice
 * screen alike. Amber, which is the token table's Apex/gold - and NOT the
 * aberrant treatment below, which bible 10.4 keeps white on purpose. */
.creature-card.founder {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: var(--reward);
}

/* bible 10.4: "Aberrant traits take an iridescent white-hot treatment...
 * Keeping it white rather than gold avoids colliding with the map's gold
 * Apex Vein pulse." White-hot here, gold on the Founder above - the two
 * markers must not converge. The spec also calls this the only animated
 * treatment in the system; the motion half is not implemented. */
.creature-card.aberrant {
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: var(--surface);
    background-color: var(--surface-raised);
}

/* AND IT IS NOW THE ONLY FILL THE SLOT EVER TAKES, which makes the marker
 * louder rather than quieter: the plate above went transparent in Phase 9
 * Task 16, so a violet plate behind the animal reads as the treatment 10.4
 * asks for instead of as a differently-tinted version of every other card. */
.creature-card.aberrant .creature-card__slot {
    background-color: var(--violet-tint);
    border-radius: 12px;
}

/* Committed to a wave: still legible, visibly not actionable. */
.creature-card.committed {
    opacity: 0.55;
}
